From: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:40:00 +0800
Subject: quirks: add upstream device entries this baseline does not cover

Backport the remaining device entries from upstream main, keeping the
package on 1.28.1 - no version bump.

Only devices that the current tree does not match at all are added, and
only where every quirk key is already understood. Verified against
upstream main by matching vendor/product id, name glob and DMI tokens;
pressure-pad coverage is already identical on both sides (25 vid:pid),
so nothing is duplicated here.

  GPD Pocket 3 Stylus        27C6:0113 tablet, pressure floor lowered to
                             24:12 - it has no ABS_DISTANCE and its
                             pressure floor of 47 is below the default
                             5% threshold, so light strokes were dropped.
  Nulea M501 Bluetooth       000E:3412 trackball - the device does not
                             name itself as a trackball and shares a
                             generic dongle name in USB mode, so
                             ModelTrackball is enabled for Bluetooth only.
  Contour RollerMouse        0B33:2000 USB receiver - same bouncing-keys
  USB Receiver               handling as the other RollerMouse models.

Ref: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/libinput/libinput/-/commits/main/quirks
Forwarded: not-needed (partial backport from upstream main)
Signed-off-by: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
---
 quirks/30-vendor-contour.quirks |  7 +++++++
 quirks/30-vendor-nulea.quirks   | 10 ++++++++++
 quirks/50-system-gpd.quirks     | 11 +++++++++++
 3 files changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/quirks/30-vendor-contour.quirks b/quirks/30-vendor-contour.quirks
--- a/quirks/30-vendor-contour.quirks
+++ b/quirks/30-vendor-contour.quirks
@@ -27,3 +27,10 @@
 MatchProduct=0x0703
 MatchUdevType=mouse
 ModelBouncingKeys=1
+
+[Contour Design RollerMouse USB Receiver]
+MatchUdevType=mouse
+MatchBus=usb
+MatchVendor=0x0B33
+MatchProduct=0x2000
+ModelBouncingKeys=1
diff --git a/quirks/30-vendor-nulea.quirks b/quirks/30-vendor-nulea.quirks
new file mode 100644
--- a/quirks/30-vendor-nulea.quirks
+++ b/quirks/30-vendor-nulea.quirks
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Do not edit this file, it will be overwritten on update
+
+# Nulea M501 does not name itself as a "Trackball"
+# In USB mode, it shares a generic dongle and name with other non-trackball
+# mice. As such, trackball quirks are enabled only for bluetooth modes.
+[Nulea M501 Bluetooth Trackball]
+MatchBus=bluetooth
+MatchVendor=0x000E
+MatchProduct=0x3412
+ModelTrackball=1
diff --git a/quirks/50-system-gpd.quirks b/quirks/50-system-gpd.quirks
--- a/quirks/50-system-gpd.quirks
+++ b/quirks/50-system-gpd.quirks
@@ -9,3 +9,14 @@
 MatchUdevType=touchpad
 MatchDMIModalias=dmi:*:svnGPD:pnG1688-08:*
 AttrInputProp=-INPUT_PROP_BUTTONPAD
+
+# The GPD stylus on the Pocket 3 has no ABS_DISTANCE and has a pressure
+# floor of 47, far below the default 5% threshold (=204/4096). Lower it to
+# 24/4096 so light strokes are still coming through.
+[GPD Pocket 3 Stylus]
+MatchBus=i2c
+MatchVendor=0x27C6
+MatchProduct=0x0113
+MatchUdevType=tablet
+MatchDMIModalias=dmi:*:svnGPD:pnG1621-02:*
+AttrPressureRange=24:12
